  "notes": "GAAP basis: governmental receipts/disbursements from the General Fund Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balance (pp5-6); business-type from Proprietary Fund Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Net Position total column (p9). Page map: trimmed p1-2 = report pp4-5 (Statement of Net Position, Total column used), p3 = Statement of Activities, p4 = governmental balance sheet, p5-6 = governmental funds statement, p7-8 = proprietary net position, p9 = proprietary income statement, p10-11 = proprietary cash flows (p11, the operating income reconciliation, was added by the v7 re-trim and holds nothing new), p12-13 = budgetary comparison cash basis (report pp32-33). Business-type reported totals: no single total printed, added operating revenue + interest income and total operating expenses + interest expense. Detail: cash-basis budget schedule covers the whole district including rural water (marked business-type); detail recorded as printed and is separate from basic-statement lines; cash-basis amounts differ from the GAAP statements. Governmental disbursements categorised by fund function: operating expenditures as general government (listed by object), project and improvement costs as natural resources/conservation. Reconciles: 3,473,156 + 3,546,198 - 2,911,885 + 10,000 = 4,117,469; business-type 1,783,148 + 262,543 - 276,888 - 10,000 = 1,758,803. Governmental balance sheet total equity differs from government-wide governmental net position as expected. Federal and state grants 509,864 (p5) split using the budgetary schedule p12 (Federal funds 45,750 + State funds 464,114, which ties exactly). Read pages 1-13 of 13 Detail investment income 131,851 (p12) mixes fund types; split into governmental 121,135 (p5) and business-type 10,716 (p9), which tie exactly."
